<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27901" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mannŭlus</span></b> , i, m.
		dim.
		1. mannus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Gallic pony</i> (post-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 4,
				2, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 24, 8</span></i>.
			†† </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mannus</span></b> , i,
				m.
			Celtic, <i>a kind of small Gallic horse, a
				coach-horse, cob</i> (used esp. for pleasure-drives): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agens mannos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					3, 1063</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si per obliquum similis sagittae (serpens)
					Terruit mannos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 27, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 1, 7, 77</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rapientibus esseda mannis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 2, 16, 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">detonsi,</span>”
				<i>with shorn manes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 8, 15: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obesi manni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 87, 9</span></i>
			.</div> †† <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mannus</span></b> , i,
				m.
			Germ. Mann, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρωπος</span>,
				<i>a god of the ancient Germans, son of
			Tuisco</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. G. 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
